One package whose types reach every destination the encoding-reflection class
names: reflection, the three standard encoders, both template packages, a
database scan target, a sort interface and a structured-logging call. Each type
declares one exported method, one unexported method, one exported tagged field,
one exported untagged field and one unexported tagged field, so the retained set
distinguishes the four. Two further files carry the cases the class rules on: a
value reached through a map of slices of pointers, and the writer of a template
execution.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/flow

go 1.27.1
-- json.go --
package flow

import "encoding/json"

// JSONPayload reaches the JSON encoder.
type JSONPayload struct {
	Name   string `json:"name"`
	Extra  int
	secret string `json:"secret"`
}

// Describe is exported.
func (p JSONPayload) Describe() string { return p.Name }

func (p JSONPayload) hidden() int { return p.Extra }

// EncodeJSON hands a value to the encoder.
func EncodeJSON(p JSONPayload) ([]byte, error) { return json.Marshal(p) }
